{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":23124,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"a6da6555d8ffc7c6ff796e52c8222f1491d7305a70e69a2f0257ea7ffa56bd24","packTokens":8261,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":173,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":981,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":6970,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's local SQLite database, with a few rows of sample data so each list has something to show\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Build the API side of the product with enforced business rules (capacity, waitlist, booking and cancellation windows, overlap, limit)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What should undo do to the stored booking, and what should it return on success?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Delete the booking row (as if it was never made) and return exactly the status and body that the contract declares for undoBooking\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When a Booked class has ended, does the booking become Attended? This affects the past list, 'classes this month' and the streak.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat it as Attended when read (derived, not stored)\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the /test simulate-other-member-cancellation hook be available in every environment?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Always map it, as the contract lists it\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Only the demo member exists, so how are other members' bookings and waitlist places represented, and how does promotion work when the demo member is not first in line (on cancel or simulate)?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Store other members as counts on the session (booked and waitlist). Promoting an anonymous first-in-line member lowers the waitlist count and moves the demo member's position up; the demo member is promoted only when they are first\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"The build runs Program.cs to write the OpenAPI document, and the code comment says nothing touches the database at startup. When and how should the SQLite schema and sample data be created?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Call EnsureCreated and seed at startup only when the database is empty, and skip this when the app is run to generate the OpenAPI document\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"After the member cancels a booking or leaves a waitlist, can they book or join the same class again? If so, does that create a new booking row?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Yes. Cancelled rows don't count for already_booked, and a new row is created\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should promotion notices (listed until acknowledged) be stored?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fields on the booking (promoted-at and notice-acknowledged)\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How much sample data should be seeded, and what dates should it use? The request says 'a few rows', but §4.3 asks for 40+ sessions over the current and next week, including full, almost-full and cancelled classes and the demo member's bookings.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Seed only a few rows (a handful of sessions plus the demo member's bookings), relative to the day the database is created\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The build must generate an OpenAPI document at App.Api/openapi/built.json whenever dotnet build runs on App.Api.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"The generated document must have the same 13 operationIds, paths, HTTP methods, parameters, request bodies, response status codes, and component schemas as contracts/openapi.yaml.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"The generated document's paths must be written without the /api prefix, matching the contract as written.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"The generated document's servers list must have url /api.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"The generated document must not include the existing GET / route.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"The GET / route must still answer with status 200 and body \\\"API is up\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml must not be edited by this process.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"The API must answer each of the 13 contract operations using the HTTP method the contract declares.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"The API must answer each operation both at the /api-prefixed path and at the path as written in the contract.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me must return status 200 with id 1, name \\\"Alex Rivera\\\", initials \\\"AR\\\", and membership \\\"Unlimited Monthly\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must return status 200 and compute today as the current Europe/London date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must return a date field equal to the supplied date parameter, or today when the parameter is absent.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must return weekStart as the Monday of the week containing the resolved date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must return canGoPreviousWeek true only when the resolved date is in the next week relative to today.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must return canGoNextWeek true only when the resolved date is in the current week relative to today.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must return 7 days from Monday to Sunday, each labelled in the format \\\"ddd d\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Each day entry must include isToday, true only for the current Europe/London date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Each day entry must include hasSessions, true when at least one session starts that day, ignoring any filters.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must return the selected day's sessions, including studio-cancelled ones, ordered by startsAt ascending.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must return status 400 with error code invalid_request when the date parameter is malformed or outside the current and next Europe/London week.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must return status 400 with error code invalid_request when type, intensity, or timeOfDay values are not in the contract's enums.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule must filter returned sessions to those matching at least one listed value of every supplied filter (type, intensity, timeOfDay), ignoring filters not supplied.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Morning must be defined as a Europe/London start before 12:00, Afternoon as 12:00 to 16:59, and Evening as 17:00 or later, for timeOfDay filtering.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Every Session response must include bookedCount and waitlistCount counting both the demo member and other members.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Every Session response must include capacityLabel formatted as \\\"{spotsLeft} of {capacity} spots left\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Every Session response must include availabilityLabel: \\\"Cancelled\\\" for studio-cancelled sessions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"availabilityLabel must be \\\"Full\\\" when a Scheduled session is full with zero on the waitlist.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"availabilityLabel must be \\\"Full · N on waitlist\\\" when a Scheduled session is full with N on the waitlist, including N=0.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"availabilityLabel must be \\\"1 spot left\\\" when exactly 1 spot remains.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"availabilityLabel must be \\\"Only N left\\\" when 2 or 3 spots remain.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"availabilityLabel must be \\\"N spots left\\\" when 4 or more spots remain.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"Each Session must include an actionState and myBookingId derived for the demo member.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"actionState must be booked (with bookingId and lateCancellation true when under 2 hours to start) when the demo member holds a Booked record, with canChange false once the class has started.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"actionState must be waitlisted (with bookingId and position) when the demo member holds a Waitlisted record, with canChange false once the class has started.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"actionState must be disabled with canChange false and reason \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\" when the demo member holds a Booked or Waitlisted record for a studio-cancelled session, checked before other disabled reasons and before examining the demo member's record type.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"When the demo member holds a Booked or Waitlisted record for a session, actionState must reflect that record (booked/waitlisted) even if the session is studio-cancelled, unless rule 35 applies first.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"actionState must be disabled with canChange false and reason \\\"Class has started\\\" when the demo member holds no record and the class has started.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"actionState must be disabled with canChange false and reason \\\"Booking opens 7 days before class\\\" when the demo member holds no record and the class starts more than 7 days away.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"actionState must be disabled with canChange false and reason \\\"Booking closes 15 minutes before class\\\" when the demo member holds no record and the class starts within 15 minutes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"actionState must be join_waitlist with position equal to waitlistCount + 1 when the demo member holds no record and the session is full.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"text\": \"actionState must be book with spotsLeft when the demo member holds no record, the session is not full, and none of the disabled conditions apply.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"text\": \"GET /sessions/{sessionId} must return status 200 with the full Session including instructor, whatToBring list, counts, labels, actionState and myBookingId, or status 404 with error code not_found when no session has that id.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"text\": \"Any request naming a sessionId or bookingId that does not exist must return status 404 with error code not_found.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings or POST /waitlist with a missing, malformed, or non-integer sessionId body must return status 400 with error code invalid_request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings for a session passing all booking rules must store a Booked record for the demo member and return status 201 with a BookingChange.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 46,\n  \"text\": \"The BookingChange's booking must have status Booked and lateCancel false; the session must show bookedCount increased by 1 and actionState booked.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 47,\n  \"text\": \"The BookingChange's message must be \\\"You're booked for {name} · {ddd HH:mm}\\\" in Europe/London time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 48,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings must return status 409 with error code cancelled_by_studio when the session is Cancelled by studio, checked first among these conditions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings must return status 409 with error code class_has_started when the session has started, checked second.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 50,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings must return status 409 with error code outside_booking_window when the session starts more than 7 days away or less than 15 minutes away, checked third.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 51,\n  \"text\": \"No booking record must be stored when POST /bookings is rejected under rules 48-50.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 52,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings or POST /waitlist must return status 409 with error code already_booked when the demo member already holds a Booked or Waitlisted record for that session, checked atomically with the insert, without storing a new record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 53,\n  \"text\": \"Cancelled records must not count toward the already_booked check, allowing a new record to be created.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings must return status 409 with error code class_full, including the refreshed Session (with actionState join_waitlist) in the error's session field, when bookedCount has reached capacity, without storing a record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 55,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings must return status 409 with error code overlap when the requested session's time range overlaps a session for which the demo member holds a Booked record, using half-open ranges so back-to-back classes do not overlap, and ignoring Waitlisted records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 56,\n  \"text\": \"The overlap error's message must be \\\"You're already booked for {name} at {HH:mm}–{HH:mm}.\\\" naming the conflicting class in Europe/London time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 57,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings must return status 409 with error code limit_reached and message \\\"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\\\" when the demo member holds 10 Booked records for sessions that have not started.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 58,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo for a Booked record no more than 5 seconds after its createdAt must delete the booking row and return status 200 with an UndoResult.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 59,\n  \"text\": \"The UndoResult's session must show counts as if the booking was never made, and its message must be \\\"Booking undone — {name}\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 60,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo must return status 409 with error code undo_expired when called more than 5 seconds after createdAt.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 61,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo must return status 409 with error code invalid_booking_state when the record is not Booked.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 62,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo must return status 404 with error code not_found for an unknown id.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 63,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel for a Booked record whose class has not started must store it as Cancelled with cancelledAt set to now.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 64,\n  \"text\": \"The cancelled record's lateCancel must be true only when the class starts less than 2 hours from now.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 65,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel must return status 200 with a BookingChange whose message begins \\\"Booking cancelled — {name}\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 66,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel must return status 409 with error code class_has_started if the class has started.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 67,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel must return status 409 with error code invalid_booking_state if the record is not Booked.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 68,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel must return status 404 with error code not_found for an unknown id.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 69,\n  \"text\": \"When cancelling a Booked record for a session with waitlistCount greater than 0, the API must promote the first anonymous waitlisted member, lowering waitlistCount by 1 and leaving bookedCount unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 70,\n  \"text\": \"When cancelling a Booked record for a session with waitlistCount equal to 0, the API must lower bookedCount by 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 71,\n  \"text\": \"POST /waitlist for a full session passing the booking rules must store a Waitlisted record with waitlistPosition equal to the previous waitlistCount + 1 and return status 201 with a BookingChange.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 72,\n  \"text\": \"The BookingChange's session must show waitlistCount increased by 1 and actionState waitlisted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 73,\n  \"text\": \"The BookingChange's message must be \\\"You're on the waitlist for {name} · {ddd HH:mm} — you're #{position}\\\" in Europe/London time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 74,\n  \"text\": \"POST /waitlist must return status 409 with error code cancelled_by_studio, class_has_started, outside_booking_window, or not_full respectively, checked in that order after the not_found and already_booked checks, without storing a record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 75,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist for a Waitlisted record whose class has not started must store it as Cancelled with lateCancel false, waitlistPosition null, and cancelledAt now, and lower the session's waitlistCount by 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 76,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist must return status 200 with a BookingChange whose message is \\\"You've left the waitlist for {name}\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 77,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist must return status 409 with error code class_has_started if the class has started.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 78,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist must return status 409 with error code invalid_booking_state if the record is not Waitlisted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 79,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist must return status 404 with error code not_found for an unknown id.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 80,\n  \"text\": \"POST /test/sessions/{sessionId}/simulate-other-member-cancellation must work in any environment.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 81,\n  \"text\": \"The simulate hook must promote the demo member to Booked, clearing waitlistPosition and recording a promoted-at timestamp, when they are first on the waitlist.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 82,\n  \"text\": \"The simulate hook must otherwise lower waitlistCount by 1 and move the demo member's waitlist position up by 1 when the waitlist is not empty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 83,\n  \"text\": \"The simulate hook must otherwise lower bookedCount by 1 when the waitlist is empty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 84,\n  \"text\": \"The simulate hook must return status 200 with a SimulationResult holding the refreshed session, with booking null when the demo member holds no Waitlisted record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 85,\n  \"text\": \"The simulate hook must return status 404 with error code not_found for an unknown session.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 86,\n  \"text\": \"When the demo member is not promoted by the simulate hook, the SimulationResult's booking must be null, and the new waitlist position must be visible through GET /sessions/{id}.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 87,\n  \"text\": \"When the demo member holds a Waitlisted record but is not first in line, the simulate hook must return that Waitlisted booking with its new waitlistPosition and list no promotion notice.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 88,\n  \"text\": \"When the demo member is promoted from a waitlist, the booking must be set to Booked even if it overlaps another Booked class or takes the demo member over 10 upcoming Booked classes, with skipReason null.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 89,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/promotion-notices must return status 200 with one notice per promoted booking that has not been acknowledged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 90,\n  \"text\": \"Each promotion notice must include bookingId, sessionId, sessionName, startsAt, and message \\\"Good news! You're off the waitlist and booked for {name} · {ddd HH:mm}\\\" in Europe/London time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 91,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/promotion-notices must not acknowledge notices when read.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 92,\n  \"text\": \"POST /me/promotion-notices/acknowledge must mark every current promotion notice as acknowledged and return status 204 with no body.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 93,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/bookings must return status 200 with an upcoming list holding Booked and Waitlisted records whose class has not ended, grouped by Europe/London day.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 94,\n  \"text\": \"Upcoming groups must be labelled \\\"Today\\\", \\\"Tomorrow\\\", or \\\"ddd d MMM\\\", in date order, with rows ordered by start time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 95,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/bookings must return a past list holding Attended, Cancelled, and Cancelled-by-studio records, ordered most recent start first.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 96,\n  \"text\": \"Each row returned by GET /me/bookings must include the contract badge (Booked, Waitlisted #N, Attended, Cancelled, Late cancel, Cancelled by studio), canChange, and isLateIfCancelledNow.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 97,\n  \"text\": \"A Booked record whose class has ended must be reported with status Attended, badge \\\"Attended\\\", and canChange false in every response, while the stored row keeps status Booked.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 98,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/stats must return status 200 with upcoming as the count of Booked records whose class has not started.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 99,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/stats must return classesThisMonth as the count of Attended records in the current Europe/London calendar month.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 100,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/stats must return currentStreakWeeks as the number of consecutive Monday-to-Sunday London weeks with at least one Attended record, counted back from the current week, or from the previous week when the current week has none yet.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 101,\n  \"text\": \"If reading or writing the database fails, or any other exception is unhandled, the API must return status 500 with an Error whose code is storage_failure and whose message is plain text without exception type names or stack trace lines.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 102,\n  \"text\": \"The API must store sessions, instructors, and the demo member's bookings in a local SQLite database (connection string App, default app.db) so changes survive an application restart.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 103,\n  \"text\": \"When the application starts normally and the database has no tables or data, the API must create the schema with EnsureCreated and insert sample data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 104,\n  \"text\": \"When data already exists, the application startup must leave it unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 105,\n  \"text\": \"When the application is run by the build to generate the OpenAPI document, it must not create, open, migrate, or seed the database.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 106,\n  \"text\": \"Seeded sample data must include sessions with instructors timed relative to the Europe/London day of seeding, including at least one session that day.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 107,\n  \"text\": \"Seeded sample data must include at least one bookable or joinable session, one full session with a waitlist, and one Cancelled by studio session.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 108,\n  \"text\": \"Seeded sample data must include demo member bookings with at least one upcoming Booked record, one Waitlisted record, and one Booked record for a class that has already ended.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 109,\n  \"text\": \"Seeding must result in today's schedule, the Upcoming list, and the Past list each returning at least one entry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 110,\n  \"text\": \"Seeded sample data must contain between 3 and 12 sessions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 111,\n  \"text\": \"Seeded sample data must contain at most 15 sessions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 112,\n  \"text\": \"The API must read the current time for every time rule, label, \\\"today\\\" value, and seed date from the TimeProvider registered in dependency injection, defaulting to the system clock.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}